ratic. The only available polls, both Democratic-sponsored and months old, show a margin-of-error race, and Polymarket prices the Democrat slightly ahead. With thin polling and a tossup consensus among raters, the evidence points to a narrow Democratic edge with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5595, "margin": 0.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5585, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.619, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5799, "margin": 1.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.557, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6133, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6185, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6098, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5891, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6068, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.615, "margin": 1.5}]}